# Next.js Frontend Consistency Standards

## 1. Code Consistency

- **Component Pattern:** Use functional arrow components exclusively. Avoid legacy class structures.
- **Strict Typing:** TypeScript strict mode is mandatory. Never bypass compile checks using the `any` type—use explicit interfaces or `unknown` combined with type guard narrowing instead.
- **Imports:** Always use defined absolute path aliases (e.g., `@/components/`) rather than fragile relative directory lookups (`../../components`).

## 2. Layout & Styles

- Rely entirely on utility framework classes for styling layouts; do not instantiate raw layout properties in isolated component CSS files.
- Enforce a strict mobile-first pattern by organizing classes using progressive responsive variants (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`).
